AB  - Urbanization profoundly impacts freshwater ecosystems. Stream restoration and enhancement can improve degraded urban streams. However, these practices are complicated by many factors. To maximize the benefits with limited resources, we need to prioritize degraded streams for intervention. The aim of this study was to develop and apply a structural equation modeling (SEM)-based tool to prioritize urban streams for enhancement in the Southeast Piedmont of the United States, a region that has experienced rapid urbanization. By applying the tool, we ranked streams according to their predicted enhancement potential. Moreover, we proposed specific enhancement scenarios for streams where we were able to meet quantitative thresholds indicating a higher rating of stream health. In addition, we identified important factors that affected the enhancement potential and threshold achievement of streams. We demonstrated the usefulness of the tool in prioritizing streams for enhancement and in developing scenarios.
